## Why not `if (Cypress.env('SMOKE'))`

```js
if (Cypress.env('SMOKE')) {
  it('login', () => { /* ... */ });
}
```

Mocha registers tests at load. Env-gated registration is brittle (tests vanish from the App, counts lie, you forget a flag). A grep plugin **filters** registered tests and reports skips/omits consistently.

DOM-conditional tests (`if (cy.get(...))` — which does not even work) are a different sin: they hide product bugs. Tags select *which tests to run*; they do not replace assertions.

## Install the grep plugin

```bash
npm install -D @cypress/grep
```

```js
// cypress/support/e2e.ts
import registerCypressGrep from '@cypress/grep';
registerCypressGrep();

// cypress.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'cypress';
import cypressGrep from '@cypress/grep/src/plugin';

export default defineConfig({
  e2e: {
    setupNodeEvents(on, config) {
      cypressGrep(config);
      return config;
    },
  },
});
```

If you only import in support *or* only in Node, tags silently do nothing. Both sides are required.

## Annotate and select

```js
it('employee can submit leave', { tags: ['@smoke', '@leave'] }, () => {
  /* ... */
});

it('okta round-trip', { tags: ['@okta', '@nightly'] }, () => {
  /* ... */
});

it('flaky balance widget', { tags: ['@flake'] }, () => {
  /* ... */
});
```

```bash
# PR job
npx cypress run --env grepTags=@smoke

# nightly: everything except flake
npx cypress run --env grepTags=-@flake
# or grepInvert=@flake depending on plugin version — read the README for the invert syntax you installed

# title grep (not tags)
npx cypress run --env grep="submit leave"
```

GitHub Actions: pass `env: CYPRESS_grepTags: '@smoke'` into `cypress-io/github-action` (11.1). The `CYPRESS_` prefix is how Cypress maps OS env to `Cypress.env` (10.2).

## Versus Playwright and Selenium

Playwright Test: `grep: /@smoke/` in config or `--grep @smoke`. pytest: `-m smoke`. JUnit 5: `@Tag("smoke")` + surefire. Learn one tagging model; the Cypress-specific part is **the grep plugin is not built-in**.

Interview line: "Cypress has no native tags. I use the grep plugin, register it in support and Node, and filter with `grepTags`. I do not `if (env)` my tests."

## The merge order you must remember

1. `env: {}` in `cypress.config.ts`
2. `cypress.env.json` (if present)
3. OS environment variables prefixed `CYPRESS_`
4. `--env key=value` on the CLI (wins)

```ts
// cypress.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  e2e: {
    baseUrl: process.env.CYPRESS_BASE_URL || 'http://localhost:3000',
    env: {
      apiUrl: 'http://localhost:4000',
      grepTags: '',
    },
  },
});
```

```json
// cypress.env.json  (gitignored)
{
  "adminPassword": "local-only"
}
```

```js
cy.request(`${Cypress.env('apiUrl')}/health`).its('status').should('eq', 200);
cy.visit('/login');
cy.get('[data-cy=password]').type(Cypress.env('adminPassword'), { log: false });
```

`{ log: false }` keeps the secret out of the Command Log and videos.

## Mapping OS env

`CYPRESS_apiUrl=https://api.staging.bizlevate.com` becomes `Cypress.env('apiUrl')`. `CYPRESS_BASE_URL` is special: it overrides `baseUrl` (config), not `env.baseUrl`. Record keys: `CYPRESS_RECORD_KEY` for Cloud (11.3).

## Multiple environments without forking specs

| Target | How |
|---|---|
| Local | default config + optional `cypress.env.json` |
| Staging CI | Actions env: `CYPRESS_BASE_URL`, `CYPRESS_apiUrl`, secrets |
| Prod smoke | separate job, read-only user, `@smoke` grep, never destructive payroll |

Optional: `configFile` is one file; people use `cypress.config.staging.ts` only if process.env branching gets unreadable. Prefer one config that reads env.

## Versus Playwright and Selenium

Playwright `projects` can encode `baseURL` + `storageState` per env in one file. Cypress typically uses **one** e2e project and lets CI mutate env. Selenium: `application.properties` / Maven profiles. Same rule: specs stay environment-agnostic.

Interview line: "Specs call `Cypress.env` and `baseUrl`. Secrets are `CYPRESS_*` or gitignored `cypress.env.json`. I never commit staging passwords or hardcode hosts."
